        "check_id": "rc-1",
        "exam": "WAEC",
        "year": null,
        "source": "authored"
      },
      "frequency": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "id": "phy_wave_optics:trap-4",
      "chapter_id": "phy_wave_optics",
      "status": "candidate",
      "section_id": "sec-3",
      "misconception": {
        "text": "Huygens' principle says that light travels in straight lines through a medium.",
        "inline": []
      },
      "correction": {
        "text": "It says every point on a wavefront acts as a source of secondary wavelets, and the later wavefront is their envelope. That is what lets light bend round an obstacle, which is diffraction.",
        "inline": []
      },
      "signal": {
        "text": "Our own question offers the reflector as an option.",
        "inline": []
      },
